        <div class="section" id="toddler">
            <h2>For a 3-Year-Old Toddler</h2>
            <p>The sky is blue because of tiny particles in the air that catch sunlight. Sunlight looks white, but it's actually made of all colors mixed together. When sunlight hits the air, the blue part of the light bounces around more than the other colors, so when we look up, we see mostly blue light coming at us. It's like when you splash water and see little blue sparkles!</p>
